Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] MSL: Preserve helper return types in geometry shaders

STEAMAC-1B, STEAMAC-1D: DXVK 2.7's dxbc-spirv compiler emits dot-product
and conversion helper functions. The fork's func_type_decl() forced every
function in a geometry module to return void, not just the geometry entry
point, so Metal rejected dp3_f32, dp4_f32, dp2_f32, f32_to_f16 and
cvt_f32_u32 (void functions returning values).

Only the geometry entry point returns void (its outputs go through the
mesh stream). Ordinary helpers, including helpers that emit vertices and
therefore receive the mesh stream, keep their SPIR-V return types.
---
 spirv_msl.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/spirv_msl.cpp b/spirv_msl.cpp
--- a/spirv_msl.cpp
+++ b/spirv_msl.cpp
@@ -16545,6 +16545,6 @@ string CompilerMSL::func_type_decl(SPIRType &type)
 {
 	auto &execution = get_entry_point();
-	if (execution.model == ExecutionModelGeometry)
+	if (processing_entry_point && execution.model == ExecutionModelGeometry)
 		return "void";
 
 	// The regular function return type. If not processing the entry point function, that's all we need
-- 
